# This tool's contract is that bytes outside comment ranges come back
# unchanged, and the test suite checks that byte for byte. Git's end-of-line
# conversion would break that claim before the tests ever run: on a Windows
# checkout with core.autocrlf=true, every LF in tests/corpus becomes CRLF, so
# the fixtures no longer hold the shapes they were written to hold.
#
# CRLF handling is tested deliberately, from string literals inside the tests
# (see `had_crlf` in src/normalize.rs and the CRLF cases in tests/cli.rs), never
# by whatever the checkout happened to produce.
* -text
